WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:03.985
So far, in this course,
our focus has been on dealing

00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:07.174
with stress by changing what
is stressful or reducing our

00:00:07.214 --> 00:00:10.830
stress levels when we cannot
change the stressful event.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.970
The next coping strategy is to encourage
you to seek out what you enjoy.

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.990
This is a proactive form of coping.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:21.654
The more positive experiences
that you have in your life,

00:00:21.694 --> 00:00:24.790
the less likely you will be
to think about your tinnitus.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.700
Many people have a tendency to focus
on what is negative in our lives.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.910
By making an effort to schedule
and then participate in pleasant events,

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.329
you are not only distracting yourself
from thinking about tinnitus,

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:40.130
but you are adding to the positive
experiences to your life.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.964
Most of us have long to-do lists,
but if you do not schedule some positive

00:00:47.004 --> 00:00:52.770
events for yourself, you may find that you
experience exhaustion and burnout.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:58.170
That may happen when we go too long at full
speed ahead without relaxing a little.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:03.056
Think about some of your favorite types
of pleasant activities and how you

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:08.510
can integrate one or two of these
activities each week into your schedule.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:12.370
Here are some examples
of planning positive events.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:17.617
Taking time to work on your favorite hobby,
such as woodworking, mechanical work,

00:01:17.657 --> 00:01:22.450
model airplane flying, fishing, gardening,
painting, cooking, sewing, or music.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:29.030
Meeting a friend somewhere to enjoy an
activity, such as food, movies, and talking.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.770
Taking time to marvel
at a beautiful sunset.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.525
Taking a trip
to your favorite nature spot,

00:01:35.565 --> 00:01:39.590
such as the beach, the coast,
the mountains, or the forest.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.713
Visiting someone whose company you enjoy,

00:01:42.753 --> 00:01:47.390
such as family members, friends,
acquaintances in the community.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:52.490
Attending an event in the community,
such as sports or theater or music.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:58.550
Carving out time to read something that you
enjoy reading, fiction or nonfiction.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.491
Taking time to savor
a good cup of coffee, tea,

00:02:02.531 --> 00:02:06.892
or other beverage at times when you
know that you can relax a little,

00:02:06.932 --> 00:02:10.670
such as after dinner or after
the children go to bed.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:17.150
We have gone over numerous forms of stress
management strategies in this section.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:20.830
You probably already have
your favorites, this is fine.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.748
Just remember that one
of the most important tips related

00:02:23.788 --> 00:02:26.990
to stress and coping is to make
sure you fit or match

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:31.030
the coping strategy with the type
of stress that you are facing.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.770
You may already be doing this
intuitively, which is great.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.210
The sections on coping
strategies are to help bring you

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:41.490
to awareness about how
to make better choices to fit

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.110
the kind of stress that you
are experiencing in your life.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:48.030
To do that in an intentional way.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:54.140
The fourth stress management
strategy is related to visualization.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:58.100
We already practiced visualization
in previous sections.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:02.940
We're going to run through another example,
which you can adopt if you like.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.820
Note that soothing music can be
played during relaxation exercises.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:13.580
Otherwise, for some people, tinnitus
becomes more noticeable in a quiet room.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.220
Now, find a relaxing
position in your chair.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:23.420
Sit in your chair with your feet
flat on the floor or propped up.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.880
Place your hands in your lap
or on the arms of the chair.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.400
Make sure you are comfortable.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.940
Take several deep breaths.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:44.140
Try to breathe deeply from your diaphragm.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:54.180
Now, imagine looking up at the sky.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:55.900
It is sunset.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:02.590
There are big puffy clouds in the sky.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:09.990
Imagine that those
clouds are your thoughts.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:15.190
These thoughts blow
around in many directions.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.880
Don't try to control these clouds.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.620
Just watch them.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.800
Observe how they drift around.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.960
Watch how the wind blows them.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:42.380
Now, watch them disappear beyond
your sight, beyond the horizon.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:52.700
Now, imagine seeing
more clouds in the sky.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:56.920
See how the sunset makes them
a beautiful reddish color.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.870
Now, watch them drift away.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.800
These clouds are like your thoughts.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:18.500
They will drift in and out of your mind.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:22.080
You do not have to control them right now.

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:31.150
Take a deep breath and then exhale.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:40.170
Feel your relaxation when you do
not try to control these clouds.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:45.110
Feel the calm and the peacefulness.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:55.580
Notice how your body feels
in this moment of peace.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:07.470
When you are ready,
count back from three to one.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:13.740
Three, become aware of your surroundings.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:23.340
Two, move your feet, legs, hands,
arms, and rotate your head.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:30.580
One, open your eyes, feeling relaxed.
